# Frontend Architecture Standard

## Preferred Architecture

Feature-Based Architecture

Example:

```text
src/
├── app/                    # Next.js App Router
│   ├── (public)/          # Route group: public pages
│   ├── (private)/         # Route group: authenticated pages
│   ├── api/               # API routes
│   └── layout.tsx         # Root layout
│
├── components/
│   ├── ui/                # shadcn/ui base components
│   ├── custom/            # Reusable custom components
│   ├── dynamic/           # Configuration-driven components
│   │   ├── dynamic-form/
│   │   ├── dynamic-table/
│   │   ├── dynamic-filter/
│   │   └── dynamic-view/
│   ├── layout/            # Layout components
│   └── providers/         # Context providers
│
├── features/              # Feature-based modules
│   ├── auth/
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   ├── hooks/
│   │   ├── services/
│   │   └── types/
│   └── [feature-name]/
│
├── hooks/                 # Shared custom hooks
├── lib/                   # Core libraries
│   └── api/               # API architecture
│       ├── modules/       # API modules
│       ├── clients/       # Client factories
│       └── registry/      # Registry pattern
├── styles/                # Global styles
├── providers/             # App-level React Context providers
├── utils/                 # Utility functions
└── constants/             # Constants

types/                     # Global TypeScript types
public/                    # Static assets
tests/
├── unit/
├── integration/
└── e2e/
```

Reason:

* Scalable
* Maintainable
* Clear ownership
* Reduced coupling
* Supports configuration-driven dynamic components

---

## Avoid

Layer-based structures that become difficult to scale.

Example:

```text
components/
pages/
services/
utils/
```

for large applications.

