# Architecture Compliance Checklist

Before approval:

* Enterprise capability baseline satisfied (mandatory tier; versions per Capability Matrix)
* TypeScript strict mode enabled
* React 19 + Next.js 15 App Router used (or ADR justifying alternative)
* shadcn/ui selected as base component library (or ADR justifying alternative)
* State management defined (local → feature → global → server state hierarchy)
* TanStack Query v5 used for server state
* React Hook Form + Zod used for forms
* Axios with interceptors used as API client
* Bun selected as package manager (or ADR justifying alternative)
* Routing strategy defined with auth guards
* Loading and error states defined for all async operations
* Security requirements addressed (NextAuth, CSP, browser storage)
* Accessibility requirements addressed (WCAG 2.1 AA considerations)
* Performance and bundle strategy defined (lazy loading, code splitting, next/image)
* Architectural patterns selected and justified (Plugin/Registry, Strategy, Config-Driven, Composition — as applicable)
* Testing strategy defined (Jest or Vitest + RTL, Playwright for E2E)
* Documentation requirements satisfied

If any item fails:

